    description: "Pass 14: entrypoints[kind=http_route] count: 8. usage_contexts[context_name=Route] count: 7. Intersection by symbol_ref/symbol_id: 7. The 1 entrypoint-only: 'HTTP WS /ws' -> python:packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/serve.py:215-250:_ws_handler:function (confidence=1.0, label='HTTP WS /ws'). The routes subcommand (when invoked with --input bm.json) correctly displays all 8 including [WS] /ws -> _ws_handler (line 215), so it reads from entrypoints not usage_contexts. Affects downstream consumers that build a route map from usage_contexts."  # 4523
    fields:  # 4523
      statement: "Every route emitted into entrypoints (kind=http_route) also appears in usage_contexts (context_name=Route) with the same symbol_id; the two registries agree on what is a route."  # 4523
      root_cause: "The route-detector emits 8 http_route entrypoints from serve.py (7 HTTP GET/POST + 1 WS /ws -> _ws_handler) but usage_contexts only captures 7 (the WS handler is excluded by usage_contexts emission policy, which apparently filters to non-WS Routes). The two registries are populated by different code paths with divergent inclusion criteria."  # 4523
